A(('p', '13.2 Neighboring parables. The Rich Fool, the Tower and the Warring King and the Narrow Door are each read in their own study of the Parable Studies. This parable makes no use of their meanings, and they make none of this one.'))
A(('p', '13.3 Final Synthesis. Jesus likens the one who hears these sayings and does them to a wise man who built his house upon a rock, and the one who hears and does not do them to a foolish man who built his house upon the sand. The rain, the floods and the winds beat on both houses. The one fell not, and the other fell, and great was the fall of it. Luke tells it with a flood and a stream, and with a man who digged deep and laid the foundation on a rock and a man who built without a foundation. Jesus names the one compared to each builder and nothing else. The comparison says that hearing is not the same as doing, that the same trial comes to both, and that what stands is what was founded.'))
